@* The site's icon set, in one place. The geometry lives in Icon.razor.cs.

   Every glyph is drawn on the same 24x24 grid with a 1.5 stroke, round caps and
   round joins, and paints with `currentColor` - so an icon inherits the colour
   of whatever it sits in, repaints with the theme toggle, and the family stays
   visually consistent the way Fluent 2 asks an icon set to.

   Inline SVG rather than an icon font or a sprite sheet: a font is a blocking
   network request this offline-first site would have to justify, and a sprite
   needs a <use> reference that a Blazor re-render would have to keep alive.

   Accessibility is decided by the CALLER, not by the glyph, because the same
   glyph is decorative in one place and meaningful in another:
     - Decorative (there is visible text beside it) -> leave Label unset; the
       svg is rendered aria-hidden.
     - Meaningful (it stands alone) -> pass Label; the svg becomes an img-role
       graphic carrying that name.
   An icon inside a button normally stays decorative and the BUTTON carries the
   accessible name, which is what the default covers.

   An unknown name renders nothing at all - a missing glyph must never be a
   missing page. *@

@if (_geometry is not null)
{
    <svg class="@Class"
         viewBox="0 0 24 24"
         width="@Size"
         height="@Size"
         fill="none"
         stroke="currentColor"
         stroke-width="1.5"
         stroke-linecap="round"
         stroke-linejoin="round"
         focusable="false"
         role="@(Label is null ? null : "img")"
         aria-hidden="@(Label is null ? "true" : null)"
         aria-label="@Label">
        @* Compile-time constants from the table in the code-behind - never a value
           that came in from a request, a query string or a user. *@
        @((MarkupString)_geometry)
    </svg>
}
